# 004-gc-interior-addresses
#
# A collection does not report a frame's addresses into heap objects
# (ADR 0120's interior roots) as roots, on either tier. Wrong only when
# such an address is the last thing keeping an object.
#
# An artificial defect for measuring the fuzzing harness (issue 681).
# Never applied to this tree: scripts/fuzz-mutant.sh applies it in a
# scratch worktree. docs/FUZZ_EVALUATION.md records what found it.
diff --git a/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs b/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs
--- a/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs
+++ b/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs
@@ -184,7 +184,8 @@
             // An address into the heap keeps the object it is inside (ADR
             // 0120): see `Space::containers`. A stack address, null included,
             // names a frame, which is not collected.
